<!-- MANUAL FIXES below, not from the exporter. urdf_joint_limits.py parses the limit tags and
     writes them onto the spawned USD prims, so these are live. -->
<!-- joint5/joint5l origins: joint5's frame had a 4.5mm Y drift; joint5l/joint6l a +/-0.001264 X
     zigzag. Both rotate about Z so only X/Y matters. link5/link5l visual+collision+inertial
     origins compensate, so no geometry moved. Same export batch as pioneer_badminton_arm and
     pioneer_boxing_arm: check those. -->
<!-- joint4/joint4l limits: swapped so each elbow's larger travel budget (+/-132.5 deg) is on its
     flexion side. The +/-75 deg rest pose and the teleop volume both bend the elbows toward +X;
     the exporter had the budgets on the hyperextension side. -->
<!-- link5..link8 (and the l links): the new forearm and wrist gripper (ArmV2_NewForearms_NewWristGrippers),
     written by step_to_links.py: meshes, inertias (1 g/cm^3 as the rest), joint6 and joint7/joint8. At
     joint5 = 0 the forearm and gripper are turned 90 deg about joint5 from the CAD (-90 right, +90 left):
     the fingers close side to side along the new MGN9 rail (base Y, 41 mm each, 0 = open), and joint6's
     axis is base -X through the joint5 axis. Joints 1-5 unchanged; check_new_gripper.py. -->
